Z||000004||RDosdorian||07-03-2001||11:49 AM||||The LT5 swap (if you can actually get it into the car) would look awesome.<P>Now, please don't jump all over me for this next comment.<P>Adding N20 and turbo(s) to it would be overkill in the Fiero.  I have a stock 1995 LT1 in my car and in that configuration, the car is a handfull to drive.  It's a lot of fun to drive, but none-the-less it is a handfull.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.goldengatefieros.org/RDosdorian_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||07-03-2001||11:51 AM||||I think you'll have one AWESOME car!<P>Good god, 425hp stock.  I hope you brought your wheelie bars! (my mustang nut friend keeps telling me I will need those with my 300hp northstar swap, heheehhehe!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||07-03-2001||12:09 PM||||375hp stock , changed to 405hp in 93 for the 40th anniversary. IT won't fit in a fiero without modifications and lots of them. It's not so much the low end grunt that is the appeal , but the top end charge. Very reliable motor , very expensive at $10,000 plus , as well replacement parts are hard to come by and expensive. Lots of power potential , but perhaps too much for a fiero tranny.<P>Also a very heavy motor. IF anyone remmebers the Vette shootout. LT1 vs ZR1 The LT1 handled better. the motor maybe all aluminum , but there's a lot of it. Keep in mind they windened the ZR1 to accomodate the motor. The latest incarnation of the vette was also designed to accept a 4 cam motor. For production costs it never came to light.<P>I can remember the 1st Zr1's cost nealry 100 grand here in Canada. When we got our 92 in 99 we paid 30 grand canadian for it. the GTS viper had a huge dent ont he king of the hill , as did the intro of the Z06.<P>Great highway car, 188mph top speed in a vette.. I don't mean to open a can of worms with old Gear ratio BS. But it does really apply to this motor , espically with a 7200rpm redline , drop in a chip and you can get 7800rpm and a 78mph 1st gear (in a vette)<P>would be quite a project , get a good tranny behind it and head to bonneville... <P><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">       <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000007||KingCobra||07-03-2001||02:24 PM||||Well I did some reserach one the car before I bought it. I figured out is was a Lingenfelter prepped 415 cid.With 610+ BHP / 500+ lbs-ft of torque. But I am still not sure about the turbo(s) and N20. With this combination what do you think this car would be capable of? ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||07-03-2001||02:45 PM||||???? Lingenfelter prepped. I would phone lingenfelter and run the VIN #'s by him. Turbo's and NOS.. There isn't a tranny that will stand up to that kind of power , not without mounting the engine longitudinal and using a 911 tranny , hewland or ZF.<P>To me this sounds like the person who said they had a twin turbo N*<P>If I'm wrong I'm sorry.<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000009||loafer87gt||07-03-2001||04:01 PM||||Christ man, even with a stock LT5 with no other forced induction you would look like one of those Ewoks in SW: ROTJ trying to ride the speeder bikes. Seriously, I would find someone with just a plain v8 and ride with them and see how fast a V8 Fiero is, trust me, its insane. I rode in a 87 GT with a stock 350 TPI and was blown away by how incredibly fast the car was.||||reg||1
